The original incident combined two different input paths. The shared parser assumes month first; booking-v3 displays a month-first hint while its form reads in the tenant's order. A parser fix alone does not fix the misleading hint.

Tenant locale and booking-form version determine the expected input order. Browser locale and the intake tag can disagree with that contract. Read the report body and reproduce the path before deciding a report is a duplicate.

<InvestigationSummary />

## Engineering outcome after the first submission

The course desk's engineering update reports “#4471 · closed 05 oct”. It marks parser **FIXED**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The parser ticket is therefore closed as completed.

It marks hint **WON'T FIX** because the **booking-v3 form was retired**. The hint ticket is closed as not planned, rather than falsely recording a hint fix. The report allocations below remain the October 4 snapshot; these later outcomes come from the [course engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows#engineering-update), not from that export. The update gives no named time zone or year in its closure label, and I have not independently tested a production deployment.

